{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' tests/terminal_app.rs\"","aggregated_output":"use std::collections::VecDeque;\nuse std::fs;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse std::process::Command;\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\nuse std::thread;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nuse work_leaf::{\n    AgentBackend, AgentError, AgentId, AgentLaunch, AgentSession, ChatMessage, CodexBackend,\n    CodexCommandConfig, CommandChat, MessageRole, PaneFocus, PromptPolicy, TerminalApp, UiMode,\n};\n\n#[test]\nfn terminal_app_new_and_chat_message_use_real_command_chat_backend() {\n    let backend = FakeBackend::new([\"launch reply\", \"follow reply\"]);\n    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\n    let mut app = TerminalApp::new(chat, 100, 40);\n\n    app.handle_bytes(b\":new implement parser\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n\n    assert_eq!(\n        app.ui().selected_agent().map(AgentId::as_str),\n        Some(\"user-1\")\n    );\n    assert_eq!(app.ui().focus(), PaneFocus::Right);\n    assert_eq!(app.ui().mode(), UiMode::Insert);\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"user-1\"));\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"launch reply\"));\n\n    app.handle_bytes(b\"please continue\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"user: please continue\"));\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"follow reply\"));\n    let backend = app.into_chat().into_backend();\n    let launches = backend.launches();\n    let sends = backend.sends();\n    assert_eq!(launches.len(), 1);\n    assert_eq!(sends.len(), 1);\n    assert_eq!(sends[0].0.as_str(), \"user-1\");\n    assert_eq!(sends[0].1, \"please continue\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn terminal_app_slash_command_from_chat_view_sends_agent_command() {\n    let backend = FakeBackend::new([\"launch reply\", \"status reply\"]);\n    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\n    let mut app = TerminalApp::new(chat, 100, 24);\n\n    app.handle_bytes(b\":new status command\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n    app.handle_bytes(b\"\\x1b/status\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n\n    assert_eq!(app.ui().mode(), UiMode::Insert);\n    assert_eq!(app.ui().focus(), PaneFocus::Right);\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"user: /status\"));\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"status reply\"));\n\n    let backend = app.into_chat().into_backend();\n    let sends = backend.sends();\n    assert_eq!(sends.len(), 1);\n    assert_eq!(sends[0].0.as_str(), \"user-1\");\n    assert_eq!(sends[0].1, \"/status\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn terminal_app_prompt_slash_command_sends_selected_agent_command() {\n    let backend = FakeBackend::new([\"launch reply\", \"status reply\"]);\n    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\n    let mut app = TerminalApp::new(chat, 100, 24);\n\n    app.handle_bytes(b\":new status command\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n    app.handle_bytes(b\"\\x1b:/status\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"user: /status\"));\n    assert!(app.render_frame().contains(\"status reply\"));\n    assert!(!app.render_frame().contains(\"unknown command chat command\"));\n\n    let backend = app.into_chat().into_backend();\n    let sends = backend.sends();\n    assert_eq!(sends.len(), 1);\n    assert_eq!(sends[0].0.as_str(), \"user-1\");\n    assert_eq!(sends[0].1, \"/status\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn terminal_app_prompt_slash_space_stays_work_leaf_command() {\n    let backend = FakeBackend::new([\"launch reply\"]);\n    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\n    let mut app = TerminalApp::new(chat, 100, 24);\n\n    app.handle_bytes(b\":new status command\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n    app.handle_bytes(b\"\\x1b:/ status\\n\");\n    app.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(1));\n\n    assert!(\n        app.transcript()\n            .iter()\n            .any(|line| line == \"work-leaf> / status\")\n    );\n    assert!(\n        app.transcript()\n            .iter()\n            .any(|line| line.contains(\"unknown command chat command `/`\"))\n    );\n\n    let backend = app.into_chat().into_backend();\n    assert!(backend.sends().is_empty());\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn terminal_app_prompt_slash_with_command_row_selected_does_not_use_stale_agent() {\n    let backend = FakeBackend::new([\"launch reply\"]);\n    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"I inspected the provisional history and resulting diff. Worktree is clean. I did not modify files, rewrite history, create commits, or run the check suite.\n\nThe seven provisional commits map cleanly into three feature slices:\n\n1. `c92a0b7..394e8aa`: terminal visual selection/yank support.\n2. `394e8aa..03c3dc7`: prompt-mode slash commands routed to the selected agent.\n3. `03c3dc7..298e0aa`: post-review feature-done prompt and chat close/reopen behavior.\n\nDeferred docs should be folded into the relevant feature commits:\n- [docs/architecture.md](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/docs/architecture.md:273) needs terminal UI notes for visual yanks, prompt slash routing, and feature-done terminal handling.\n- [docs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/docs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:87) needs the old “mark review chat done” wording updated to the current patch-agent `work-leaf: Is this feature done? yes/no` flow.\n\n**Proposed Three-Commit Plan**\n1. `ADD terminal visual yanks so users can copy pane text`\n   Fold `0941cc5` + `394e8aa`. Includes [src/ui.rs::VisualKind](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/src/ui.rs:178), visual-mode key handling/yanking, OSC52 clipboard output, `TerminalAppCore` visual-context preparation, and UI/terminal tests. Add `docs/architecture.md` terminal UI documentation for `v`, `V`, Ctrl-V, `y/Y`, highlighting, and OSC52 copy behavior.\n\n2. `ADD prompt slash routing so selected agents receive commands`\n   Fold `c31fc83` + `03c3dc7`. Includes [WorkLeafController::execute_command_line](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/src/workspace.rs:129), controller selected-agent tracking, [TerminalAppCore::handle_command_line](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/src/terminal_app.rs:641), stale-command-row protection, and workspace/terminal/harness tests. Add `docs/architecture.md` notes that `/command` prompt input routes to the selected agent only when a non-space slash command and selected agent exist.\n\n3. `ADD review completion prompts so users can close finished patch chats`\n   Fold `21fc946` + `5c8ae41` + `298e0aa`. Includes [FEATURE_DONE_PROMPT](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/src/workspace.rs:18), review-complete prompt appending/selection, duplicate prompt allowance for repeated reviews, [TerminalAppCore::handle_feature_done_reply](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/src/terminal_app.rs:849), hidden-chat reopen behavior, [TerminalUi::hide_agent](/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/direct/work-leaf-3feature-sequential-bench.Uzex9B/repo/src/ui.rs:390), and review/workspace/terminal tests. Update both docs files so the review lifecycle describes the patch-agent completion prompt and `yes/y` terminal close behavior.\n\nAfter acceptance, I’ll rebuild the history rooted at `c92a0b7060a36eac6db2d869b85e589a7a9480f9` with exactly those three commits, then run the required validation suite and real-agent verification. Waiting for acceptance."}}
